Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Everyone:

I am trying to implement a multiscale occupancy framework just as mentioned in the chapter 10.10 of the AHM book. I have data collected through camera traps that where nested inside 1x1 km grids, but due to the limited number of cameras I first surveyed a set of grids for 30 days, and then relocated the cameras in other grids to have a bigger number surveyed sites. Because of this design, I have many NAs in my observation data and also in my covariates related with detection probability.

I know that this occupancy models can deal with missing data in the observations, nevertheless, it seems like the model cannot deal with missing values of covariates. Every time I run my script using the function JagsUI, I get the next error:
Unable to resolve the following parameters: p.sensor[1,1,7] (line 35),  p.sensor[1,1,8] (line 35)...

Does anyone know how can I solve this problem? I would really appreciate if someone can give me any advice.

Thank you so much.

